{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790260763725,"sessionID":"ses_f2c26c40bffeGVWBaBnfuNUxb0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_62b276c54eec44cba10a1afa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The full directory structure (all files and folders)\n2. The contents of scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn if it exists\n3. The contents of scenes/main.tscn if it exists\n4. The contents of scripts/generic_effect_handler.gd if it exists\n5. The contents of assets/shaders/muzzle_flash.gdshader if it exists\n6. Any other relevant files like project.godot or other scripts\n\nReturn the full contents of all these files. Be very thorough.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f2c2676c1ffeHNE0RC13Fmt0ko\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is the complete exploration of the `/workspace` directory.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Full Directory Structure\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore                              (empty file)\n│   ├── uid_cache.bin                          (binary)\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg                 (empty file)\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   ├── filesystem_cache10\n│   │   ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│   │   └── project_metadata.cfg\n│   └── imported/                              (empty directory)\n├── assets/\n│   └── shaders/\n│       ├── muzzle_flash.gdshader\n│       └── muzzle_flash.gdshader.uid\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── main.tscn\n│   └── effects/\n│       └── muzzle_flash_effect.tscn\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── generic_effect_handler.gd\n│   └── generic_effect_handler.gd.uid\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\nThere are **17 files** in total (including `.godot` metadata and UID files). The project is a **Godot 4.4** project using the GL compatibility renderer.\n\n---\n\n## 2. `/workspace/scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn`\n\n```\n[gd_scene format=3 uid=\"uid://task0620_start_effect\"]\n\n[node name=\"MuzzleFlashEffect\" type=\"Node3D\"]\n```\n\nThis is a minimal scene -- just a bare `Node3D` root node named `MuzzleFlashEffect`. It has no children, no attached script, and no resources. It is essentially a placeholder ready to be built out.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`\n\n```\n[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3 uid=\"uid://task0620_start_main\"]\n\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" path=\"res://scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn\" id=\"1_e4p0h\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node3D\"]\n\n[node name=\"Camera3D\" type=\"Camera3D\" parent=\".\"]\ntransform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 3)\n\n[node name=\"MuzzleFlashEffect\" parent=\".\" instance=ExtResource(\"1_e4p0h\")]\n```\n\nThis is the main scene. It has:\n- A root `Node3D` called `Main`.\n- A `Camera3D` child positioned at `(0, 0, 3)`.\n- An instanced child `MuzzleFlashEffect` referencing `muzzle_flash_effect.tscn` via `ExtResource(\"1_e4p0h\")`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `/workspace/scripts/generic_effect_handler.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node3D\n\n@export_node_path(\"Light3D\") var optional_light_path: NodePath\n@export var light_duration := 0.2\nvar optional_light: Light3D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\toptional_light = get_node_or_null(optional_light_path)\n\tvar max_duration := 0.0\n\tfor child in get_children():\n\t\tif child is GPUParticles3D:\n\t\t\tvar particles := child as GPUParticles3D\n\t\t\tmax_duration = max(max_duration, particles.lifetime)\n\t\t\tparticles.one_shot = true\n\t\t\tparticles.emitting = true\n\t\telif child is CPUParticles2D:\n\t\t\tvar cpu := child as CPUParticles2D\n\t\t\tmax_duration = max(max_duration, cpu.lifetime)\n\t\t\tcpu.one_shot = true\n\t\t\tcpu.emitting = true\n\n\tif optional_light:\n\t\tvar tween := create_tween()\n\t\ttween.tween_property(optional_light, \"light_energy\", 0.0, light_duration)\n\t\tif optional_light is OmniLight3D:\n\t\t\ttween.tween_property(optional_light, \"omni_range\", 0.0, light_duration)\n\n\tvar wait_time := max_duration if max_duration > 0.01 else 0.1\n\tget_tree().create_timer(wait_time).timeout.connect(queue_free)\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- Extends `Node3D`.\n- Has an exported `NodePath` to an optional `Light3D` and a `light_duration` export (default `0.2` seconds).\n- On `_ready`:\n  1. Resolves the optional light.\n  2. Iterates all children -- if a child is `GPUParticles3D` or `CPUParticles2D`, it sets them to `one_shot = true`, starts emitting, and tracks the maximum particle `lifetime`.\n  3. If a light was found, it creates a tween that fades `light_energy` to 0 (and also `omni_range` if it's an `OmniLight3D`) over `light_duration`.\n  4. After the max particle lifetime (or 0.1s fallback), the node calls `queue_free()` to clean itself up.\n\n---\n\n## 5. `/workspace/assets/shaders/muzzle_flash.gdshader`\n\n```glsl\nshader_type spatial;\nrender_mode unshaded, cull_disabled, depth_draw_always;\n\nuniform vec4 flash_color : source_color = vec4(1.0);\nuniform float falloff_power : hint_range(0.1, 4.0) = 1.0;\n\nvoid fragment() {\n\tfloat radial = 1.0 - length(UV - vec2(0.5));\n\tradial = clamp(radial, 0.0, 1.0);\n\tfloat mask = pow(radial, falloff_power);\n\tALBEDO = flash_color.rgb;\n\tALPHA = mask;\n\tEMISSION = ALBEDO * 4.0 * mask;\n}\n```\n\n**What it does:**\n- `spatial` shader with `unshaded`, `cull_disabled`, and `depth_draw_always` render modes.\n- Two uniforms: `flash_color` (default white, `source_color` hint) and `falloff_power` (range 0.1-4.0, default 1.0).\n- The fragment shader computes a radial gradient from the center of the UV space, applies an alpha mask with a power falloff, and emits the flash color multiplied by 4.0 and by the mask intensity.\n- Because `cull_disabled` is set, it renders from both sides.\n\n---\n\n## 6. All Other Files\n\n### `/workspace/project.godot`\n```ini\n; Engine configuration file.\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"Build the muzzle flash effect prefab\"\nconfig/description=\"A simple task to test CUA ability to move a player asset to the origin coordinates\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[rendering]\n\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n- Godot 4.4 project.\n- Named \"Build the muzzle flash effect prefab\".\n- Main scene is `res://scenes/main.tscn`.\n- Uses the GL compatibility renderer.\n\n### `/workspace/task_config.json`\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Create a layered muzzle flash prefab: edit scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn so the root Node3D uses scripts/generic_effect_handler.gd, targets its Optional Light export at an OmniLight child named MuzzleFlash, and keeps a 0.2 second fade. Add SmokeParticles configured with zero gravity and a StandardMaterial3D mesh using a radial GradientTexture2D. Simulate a volumetric smoke puff via using particle billboard mode for billboarding, plus a pair of opposing GPUParticles3D named MuzzleFireLeft and MuzzleFireRight that emit one-shot bursts. Each muzzle fire particle system must rely on the provided assets/shaders/muzzle_flash.gdshader ShaderMaterial and include a draw-pass QuadMesh so the burst renders from both sides. Wire the scene into scenes/main.tscn so Main instantiates the finished effect.\"\n}\n```\n- This is the task instruction describing what needs to be built: a layered muzzle flash prefab with smoke particles and two opposing GPU particle systems, all wired into `main.tscn`.\n\n### `/workspace/scripts/generic_effect_handler.gd.uid`\n```\nuid://1fwasvyf0jja\n```\n\n### `/workspace/assets/shaders/muzzle_flash.gdshader.uid`\n```\nuid://b8mloxgyn13ly\n```\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/editor/project_metadata.cfg`\n```ini\n[editor_metadata]\nexecutable_path=\"/run/gamedevbench-bin/godot\"\n\n[recent_files]\nscenes=[\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"]\n```\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/editor/main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg`\n```ini\n[folding]\nnode_unfolds=[NodePath(\"Camera3D\"), PackedStringArray(\"Transform\")]\nresource_unfolds=[]\nnodes_folded=[]\n```\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/editor/filesystem_cache10`\n```\nea4bc82a6ad023ab7ee23ee620429895\n::res://::1790260615\ntask_config.json::JSON::-1::1790260615::0::1::::<><><>0<>0<><>::\n::res://assets/::1790260615\n::res://assets/shaders/::1790260615\nmuzzle_flash.gdshader::Shader::4728119163246743710::1790255209::0::1::::<><><>0<>0<><>::\n::res://scenes/::1790260615\nmain.tscn::PackedScene::-1::1790255209::0::1::::<><><>0<>0<><>::res://scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn\n::res://scenes/effects/::1790260615\nmuzzle_flash_effect.tscn::PackedScene::-1::1790255209::0::1::::<><><>0<>0<><>::\n::res://scripts/::1790260615\ngeneric_effect_handler.gd::GDScript::1836568576159323566::1790255209::0::1::::<>Node3D<><>0<>0<><>::\n```\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg`\n```\nlist=[]\n```\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg`\n(empty file)\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/.gdignore`\n(empty file)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a **Godot 4.4** project with the **GL compatibility** renderer, focused on building a **muzzle flash effect prefab**. The key files are:\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `/workspace/project.godot` | Project configuration, main scene entry point |\n| `/workspace/task_config.json` | Task instructions describing the full prefab to build |\n| `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` | Main scene with Camera3D and instanced MuzzleFlashEffect |\n| `/workspace/scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn` | Skeletal template scene (bare Node3D) to be built out |\n| `/workspace/scripts/generic_effect_handler.gd` | Auto-starting particle + light fade handler script |\n| `/workspace/assets/shaders/muzzle_flash.gdshader` | Radial flash shader with unshaded emission, two-sided rendering |\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f2c26c40bffeGVWBaBnfuNUxb0","sessionId":"ses_f2c2676c1ffeHNE0RC13Fmt0ko","m